            ],
            "aiSupplement": {
              "explanation": [
                {
                  "text": "A standard dihybrid expectation assumes appropriate dominance relationships and independent inheritance. Linkage or interactions between genes can change the expected classes, while sampling and environmental effects can alter observed proportions.",
